```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor ClientA as Bidder Client A
    actor ClientB as Bidder Client B
    participant Server as BidNetServer
    participant HandlerA as ClientHandler (A)
    participant Auth as AuthService
    participant Router as MessageRouter
    participant Engine as BidProcessor
    participant Auction as Auction (A-999)
    participant Bcast as BroadcastManager
    participant DB as MongoDB (Async Worker)

    Note over ClientA, Server: Phase 1: TCP Handshake & Authentication
    ClientA->>Server: TCP Connect (Port 5000)
    Server-->>HandlerA: Spawn Handler in ThreadPool
    ClientA->>HandlerA: LOGIN {"username":"UserA", "password":"***"}
    HandlerA->>Router: route(rawJson)
    Router->>Auth: handleLogin()
    Auth->>Auth: BCrypt Verify Credentials
    Auth-->>ClientA: LOGIN_RESPONSE {"success":true}

    Note over ClientA, Server: Phase 2: Join Auction Room
    ClientA->>HandlerA: JOIN_AUCTION (A-999)
    HandlerA->>Bcast: subscribe("A-999", "UserA")
    HandlerA-->>ClientA: AUCTION_UPDATE (Current state)

    Note over ClientA, ClientB: Phase 3: Critical Section Bidding
    ClientA->>HandlerA: PLACE_BID {"amount": 250000.0}
    HandlerA->>Router: route(PLACE_BID)
    Router->>Engine: process(msg)
    Engine->>Auction: lock.lock() (Fair ReentrantLock)
    Note over Auction: Critical Section Active
    Engine->>Auction: Validate 5% min increment
    Engine->>Auction: updateBid(250000.0, "UserA")
    Engine->>Auction: lock.unlock() (finally block)

    Note over Engine, ClientB: Phase 4: Non-blocking Broadcast & Async DB Persist
    par TCP Real-time Fan-out
        Engine->>Bcast: broadcastUpdate(auction)
        Bcast-->>ClientA: AUCTION_UPDATE {"currentBid":250000, "highestBidder":"UserA"}
        Bcast-->>ClientB: AUCTION_UPDATE {"currentBid":250000, "highestBidder":"UserA"}
    and Asynchronous Write
        Engine-)DB: saveBidAsync("A-999", "UserA", 250000.0)
    end
```
